4bc-9c95-2b343e22fdf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-75717" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $CB=BC$\n- $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- $A(BC)=(AB)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\nTherefore, only statement  III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75717/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75717"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275521/field-1/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" :answer/id #uuid "de607e2a-211a-52fe-ba2a-cf20880ffd04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275521/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "f578abb2-5d28-59c8-97d1-9e040b6a545e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275521/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a362a355-9b78-59e9-92d2-5b9079a83718" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275521/field-1/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" :answer-field/choices ["q-275521/field-1/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" "q-275521/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275521/field-2/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a6